[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kototama.tender's host-import module name was wrongly \"kototama\" -- fixed to \"kotoba\" (kotoba.runtime's WASM encoder hardcodes this for every real compiled guest; the WAT test fixtures only ever passed against themselves, never a real compiled guest)" "aiueos.execute/launcher (JVM-only, found already implementing a similar Chicory-hosted capability-gated execution idea under aiueos's own manifest/broker vocabulary) is NOT adopted as a kototama.tender replacement -- consolidation on the JVM substrate is deliberately deferred, not decided here" "kototama.contract's actor:host ABI lands on the BROWSER-native substrate first (actor-host.js in kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent, plain JS matching that repo's existing zero-build-step convention), per the owner's .cljc runtime priority (kototama > cljs > nbb > jvm)" "kototama's web/index.html is now generated via kotoba-lang/html + kotoba-lang/css (Hiccup EDN -> HTML/CSS) run under nbb (generate.cljs), applying the same .cljc priority rule to authoring the page itself, not just guest-side logic" "ADDENDUM (same day): :now/:log-append! renamed to :clock-monotonic/:log-write across kototama.contract, kototama.tender, and wasm-webcomponent's actor-host.js, to reuse names a concurrent session had already independently registered in kotoba-core-contracts' shared capability_contract.edn for aiueos's kernel-capability vocabulary (identical wire signatures) -- rather than registering the same operation twice under different names in a table every .kotoba guest shares (kototama#21, wasm-webcomponent#3, kototama#22)" "ADDENDUM (same day): gen-keypair/sign/verify also landed browser-native (wasm-webcomponent vendored the real @noble/curves Ed25519 -- pure arithmetic, not I/O, so it never needed the async Web Crypto API this ADR's original \"NOT implemented\" reasoning was about) -- 7 of 8 actor:host imports are now browser-implemented, only http-post remains impossible; this ADR's original \"4 of 8\" / hand-rolled-Ed25519-follow-up claims are superseded"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kototama-actor-host-browser-native-and-tender-module-fix", :adr/related ["adr-2607062330" "adr-2607022400" "adr-2607022900" "adr-2607061630"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607062400-kototama-actor-host-browser-native-and-tender-module-fix", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-06", :adr/body "see 2607062400-kototama-actor-host-browser-native-and-tender-module-fix.edn", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/artifacts "{:kototama \"kotoba-lang/kototama (module-name fix + web/ regenerated via generate.cljs; PR #21 clock-monotonic/log-write rename, PR #22 web/ pin bump) — 18 tests/35 assertions green (JVM), 3 smoke tests green (Node)\", :wasm-webcomponent \"kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent (actor-host.js added; PR #3 clock-monotonic/log-write rename + vendored ed25519 gen-keypair/sign/verify already landed independently) — 17 checks green in verify-actor-host.mjs, real native-WebAssembly round trip\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-06", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607062400: kototama's actor:host ABI lands browser-native (priority target), kototama.tender's module-name bug fixed", :adr/source-format "edn"}]